  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Dealer deals all 40 cards (e.g. 10 each in the four-player game), one at a time face down; the last card is turned for trump. Player to dealer's right leads. Players must follow suit and, when possible, beat the highest card so far in the trick; if unable to follow suit they must trump and overtake if able. Trick winner leads next. After winning a trick a player may sing one or more 20s or 40s (king and jack of same suit) before leading. When all cards are played, points in tricks, singing, and last trick are counted; higher total wins the deal.",
    Player: "Dealer deals all 40 cards (e.g. 10 each in the four-player game), one at a time face down; the last card is turned for trump. Player to dealer's right leads. Players must follow suit and, when possible, beat the highest card so far in the trick; if unable to follow suit they must trump and overtake if able. Trick winner leads next. After winning a trick a player may sing one or more 20s or 40s (king and jack of same suit) before leading. When all cards are played, points in tricks, singing, and last trick are counted; higher total wins the deal.",
    objective: 'Win tricks containing high-value cards and score points from card values, singing (king and jack of same suit for 20 or 40 points), and the last trick (10 points). The team or player with more points wins the deal; in match play the side that wins more deals wins.',
    gameplay: "Dealer deals all 40 cards (e.g. 10 each in the four-player game), one at a time face down; the last card is turned for trump. Player to dealer's right leads. Players must follow suit and, when possible, beat the highest card so far in the trick; if unable to follow suit they must trump and overtake if able. Trick winner leads next. After winning a trick a player may sing one or more 20s or 40s (king and jack of same suit) before leading. When all cards are played, points in tricks, singing, and last trick are counted; higher total wins the deal.",
    keyRules: [
      'Use 40-card Spanish deck; in Guiñote jack ranks above horse and is worth 3 points, horse 2.',
      'Trump determined by turned card; follow suit and overtake when possible; must trump if cannot follow.',
      'Sing 20 (king and jack of non-trump suit) or 40 (king and jack of trumps) after winning a trick; 40 must be declared before 20; multiple declarations allowed after one trick in Guiñote.',
      'No tute (four kings or four horses) validity in Guiñote. Winner of last trick deals next hand.',
    ],
