    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win tricks containing high-value cards and score points from card values, singing (king and jack of same suit for 20 or 40 points), and the last trick (10 points). The team or player with more points wins the deal; in match play the side that wins more deals wins.',
      "Turn-flow example: Dealer deals all 40 cards (e.g. 10 each in the four-player game), one at a time face down; the last card is turned for trump. Player to dealer's right leads. Players must follow suit and, when possible, beat the highest card so far in the trick; if unable to follow suit they must trump and overtake if able. Trick winner leads next. After winning a trick a player may sing one or more 20s or 40s (king and jack of same suit) before leading. When all cards are played, points in tricks, singing, and last trick are counted; higher total wins the deal.",
      'Scoring example: Count card points in won tricks (Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Jack 3, Horse 2), add 10 for last trick, add 20 or 40 for each sung combination. Higher total wins the deal. The team or player with more total points (cards in tricks, singing, and 10 for last trick) wins the deal. If tied, the side that won the last trick wins..',
